@startuml
title RK01 black-box class architecture
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Application black box" {
  class Application <<client firmware>> {
    +constructBootGraph()
    +startTasks()
  }

  class Domain <<writable authority>> {
    +allocate()
    +attachSharedMemory()
  }

  class Task <<unprivileged actor>> {
    +run()
    +callKernelApi()
  }

  class DomainRam <<persistent state>> {
    +sameDomainReadWrite()
  }

  class TaskStack <<private state>> {
    +mappedForOwnerOnly()
  }

  class SharedMemory <<explicit aperture>> {
    +attach(domain)
    +getRegion()
  }
}

package "Public boundary" {
  class KernelApi <<k* facade>> {
    +createTask()
    +createDomain()
    +createObject()
    +sendMessage()
    +sleepOrDelay()
    +logOrDiagnose()
  }

  class SyscallGateway <<SVC boundary>> {
    +validateOrigin()
    +validateHandle()
    +validateUserBuffers()
    +enterPrivilegedService()
  }
}

package "Privileged RK01 core" {
  class Kernel <<trusted core>> {
    +initialize()
    +dispatch()
    +applyMpuView()
  }

  class Scheduler <<service>> {
    +selectNextTask()
    +blockOrReady()
  }

  class ObjectRegistry <<service>> {
    +resolveHandle()
    +trackGeneration()
  }

  class IpcServices <<service>> {
    +copyPayload()
    +queueMessage()
    +callReply()
  }

  class SyncServices <<service>> {
    +lockMutex()
    +pendSemaphore()
    +sleepQueue()
  }

  class TimerServices <<service>> {
    +scheduleTimeout()
    +runCallout()
  }

  class FaultServices <<service>> {
    +recordFault()
    +containTaskFault()
    +postProcessCleanup()
  }

  class Diagnostics <<service>> {
    +nameObjects()
    +snapshotTrace()
  }
}

package "Trusted platform and services" {
  class BoardPort <<trusted port>> {
    +startup()
    +configureClock()
    +configureMpu()
    +handleExceptions()
  }

  class ConsoleService <<privileged service>> {
    +writeBounded()
    +ownForegroundRx()
  }

  class FileSystemService <<optional middleware>> {
    +mount()
    +read()
    +write()
  }
}

Application "1" o-- "1..*" Domain : declares
Domain "1" *-- "1..*" Task : schedules members
Domain "1" *-- "1" DomainRam : maps writable window
Task "1" *-- "1" TaskStack : owns private stack
Domain "0..*" o-- "0..*" SharedMemory : explicit attachment

Application --> KernelApi : public construction and runtime calls
Task --> KernelApi : k* calls
KernelApi --> SyscallGateway : unprivileged callers cross SVC
SyscallGateway --> Kernel : checked privileged operation

Kernel *-- Scheduler
Kernel *-- ObjectRegistry
Kernel *-- IpcServices
Kernel *-- SyncServices
Kernel *-- TimerServices
Kernel *-- FaultServices
Kernel *-- Diagnostics

Kernel --> BoardPort : HAL and MPU hooks
ConsoleService --> BoardPort : UART/device access
FileSystemService --> BoardPort : flash backend
Application --> ConsoleService : optional trusted endpoint
Application --> FileSystemService : optional RKFS facade

Task ..> DomainRam : direct only in same domain
Task ..> SharedMemory : direct only when attached
Task ..> Task : copied IPC, events, call/reply
IpcServices --> ObjectRegistry : resolve handles
SyncServices --> ObjectRegistry : resolve handles
TimerServices --> ObjectRegistry : resolve handles
FaultServices --> Scheduler : remove faulted task
Diagnostics --> ObjectRegistry : inspect named objects

note top of KernelApi
  This is the stable black-box surface:
  public k* APIs hide kernel object storage.
end note

note right of Domain
  A domain is a writable-authority boundary,
  not a process, loader, or file-table namespace.
end note

note bottom of SyscallGateway
  SVC validation checks handles, caller mode,
  buffers and function pointers before privileged use.
end note
@enduml
